{
    "id": "07",
    "title": "Exception Handling",
    "content": "<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.12) 0%, rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.04) 100%); border: 1px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.2); border-left: 4px solid #EF4444; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 60px; border-radius: 4px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"position: absolute; top: -20px; right: -20px; opacity: 0.05; transform: rotate(15deg);\"><svg width=\"120\" height=\"120\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#EF4444\" stroke-width=\"1\"><path d=\"M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"9\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"13\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"12.01\" y2=\"17\"/></svg></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text-heading); font-weight: 300;\">Photon implements a <strong>Fail-Safe Execution Kernel</strong>. We guarantee that a single crashing request will never compromise the stability or performance of the entire system.</p></div><h2>Isolation Architecture</h2><p>Error handling in Photon is decoupled from the main event loop. Every exception is trapped within a scoped boundary, ensuring atomic state management and memory safety.</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 24px; margin: 48px 0;\" class=\"bento-grid\"><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(239,64,64,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"> <div style=\"color: #EF4444; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">ERROR_TRAP</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">JIT-optimized try-catch boundaries that capture runtime failures with zero measurable overhead on successful requests.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(239,64,64,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #EF4444; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M21 2l-2 2m-7.61 7.61a5.5 5.5 0 1 1-7.778 7.778 5.5 5.5 0 0 1 7.777-7.777zm0 0L15.5 7.5m0 0l3 3L22 7l-3-3-3.5 3.5z\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">ATOMIC_RESET</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Failed requests trigger an immediate header flush and context wipe, effectively rolling back the state before error delivery.</p></div><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; border-radius: 4px; transition: all 0.3s ease;\" onmouseover=\"this.style.borderColor='rgba(239,64,64,0.4)'; this.style.transform='translateY(-4px)'\" onmouseout=\"this.style.borderColor='var(--border-subtle)'; this.style.transform='translateY(0)'\"><div style=\"color: #EF4444; margin-bottom: 20px;\"><svg width=\"32\" height=\"32\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><line x1=\"22\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"18\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"6\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"2\" y2=\"12\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"2\"/><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"22\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"18\"/></svg></div><h3 style=\"margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; tracking: 0.05em; border: none; padding: 0;\">TYPED_ALARM</h3><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.8; padding: 0; border: none;\">Seamless integration with custom classes. Photon uses instance-of checks for high-speed error categorization.</p></div></div><h2>Global Orchestration</h2><p>The <code>onError</code> matrix allows you to define a centralized logic for failure resolution. Whether it's a validation mismatch or a database timeout, the resolution is unified.</p><pre><code>app.onError((err, c) => {\n  const telemetryId = c.get('trace_id')\n  \n  if (err instanceof ValidationException) {\n    return c.json({ error: 'DATA_MISMATCH', fields: err.errors }, 422)\n  }\n  \n  return c.json({ \n    status: 'SYSTEM_ERROR', \n    ref: telemetryId \n  }, 500)\n})</code></pre><div style=\"background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.05); border: 1px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.1); border-left: 4px solid #EF4444; padding: 24px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><h4 style=\"margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 900; color: #EF4444; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;\">// SYSTEM_LOG: RECOVERY_DYNAMICS</h4><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; color: var(--text-heading); opacity: 0.9; border: none; padding: 0;\">Photon handles unhandled rejections automatically. Even if a third-party promise fails within your handler, the <strong>Global Guard</strong> will prevent the Bun process from exiting.</p></div><h2>Propagation Analysis</h2><p>Response latency during error propagation. Photon ensures that error delivery is almost as fast as a standard response.</p><div style=\"background: var(--surf-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding: 32px; margin: 40px 0; border-radius: 4px;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom: 30px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #EF4444; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>PHOTON_INTERNAL_EXCEPTION_PATH</span> <span>< 0.005ms</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(239,68,68,0.1); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 5%; background: #EF4444; box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(239,68,68,0.5);\"></div></div></div><div style=\"margin-bottom: 30px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; color: #6B7280; margin-bottom: 12px; font-family: var(--font-technical);\"><span>CONSTRUCTION_OVERHEAD (Standard Error)</span> <span>0.15ms</span></div><div style=\"height: 8px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05); width: 100%; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden;\"><div style=\"height: 100%; width: 80%; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);\"></div></div></div><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; font-family: var(--font-technical); border: none; padding: 0;\">// METRIC: HIGH-SPEED DISPATCH EVEN UNDER EXTREME LOAD</p></div><h2>Custom Exception Logic</h2><p>Extend the base <code>Error</code> class to create rich, context-aware exceptions that carry additional metadata through the pipeline.</p><pre><code>class BusinessError extends Error {\n  constructor(public code: string, message: string) {\n    super(message)\n    this.name = 'BusinessError'\n  }\n}\n\n// Trigger in handler\napp.post('/api/pay', async (c) => {\n  if (balance < amount) {\n    throw new BusinessError('LOW_FUNDS', 'Insufficient balance')\n  }\n})</code></pre><div style=\"background: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(59, 130, 246, 0.1), transparent); border-left: 4px solid #3B82F6; padding: 24px; margin-top: 60px; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; font-style: italic; border: none; padding: 0; color: var(--text-heading);\"><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Use the <code>notFound</code> handler specifically for SPA fallbacks. If the client requests <code>text/html</code>, return your index.html; for everything else, return an atomic 404 JSON.</p></div>",
